# {{name}}

A Pterodactyl panel theme, scaffolded by `p:extension:make --theme`. The "Themes" chapter of the
SDK README (`node_modules/@pterodactyl/sdk/README.md`) documents everything used here: the
manifest, the stylesheet and tokens, skins, views, the workbench, the CLI and the test helpers.

## Files

| File | |
| --- | --- |
| `extension.json` | The manifest. `"type": "theme"` and its `theme` section declare the stylesheet, the colour schemes and the settings administrators change on the Themes page. |
| `src/theme.css` | The panel stylesheet with this theme's tokens and classes. It starts with `@import '@pterodactyl/sdk/theme-entry.css';` and replaces the panel's stylesheet. Plain Tailwind, no prefix. |
| `src/theme.tsx` | `defineTheme`: skins for the UI kit and views by name. |
| `src/skins.ts` | Class recipes for UI primitives such as `Button` and `Card`. |
| `src/views/AppLayout.tsx` | A layer over classic's app layout. |
| `src/theme.spec.tsx` | Renders views and primitives with the theme through `@pterodactyl/sdk/testing`. |

Each setting writes a CSS token (`token`), an `<html>` attribute (`attribute`), or both, before the
page renders. `npm run types` writes `src/theme-types.ts`, whose `ThemeSettings` types
`useThemeSettings<ThemeSettings>()`.

## Scripts

| Script | |
| --- | --- |
| `npm run build` | `dist/client.js`, `dist/theme.css` and `dist/theme.json`. |
| `npm run dev` | Rebuilds on change; `p:extension:dev --watch` runs it. |
| `npm run typecheck` | Checks the theme against the SDK's types. |
| `npm test` | Runs the tests. |
| `npm run doctor` | The panel's checks: manifest, build, budgets, remote URLs and view names. |
| `npm run types` | Generates `src/theme-types.ts` from the settings. |
| `npm run pack` | Packs a `.pteroext` archive to install on another panel. |

## Develop

```sh
npm install
php {{artisan}} p:extension:dev . --enable
php {{artisan}} p:theme:activate {{id}}
php {{artisan}} p:extension:dev . --watch
```

The first command builds, installs and enables the theme. While the last one runs on a panel with
`APP_DEBUG=true`, a change to `src/theme.css` swaps into open pages without a reload, and any other
change reloads them. `/panel/theme-workbench` renders every view and primitive from fixtures.
